> good a place as any.
> 
> Yet sooner or later I expect to find another Priest, and will have to
> come back to Fort Ludios. What is the best way to avoid traps?

The guaranteed best way is not to move! ;-)

Wands of secret door detection help to detect nearby traps. Scrolls of
gold detection that you read while confused detects them on the level.
There are other possibilities, too.

But traps are there to surprise the victim, so every powerful way to
detect them is not applicable for long, is limited by the ressources
(objects and charges) you have.

Therefore the best way is to use tools that increase the probability
to find them without volatile ressources; use a ring of searching,
Excalibur, and such. Or do a manual search in case you know where the
traps might be (e.g. as in the treasure room of Croesus).

> My
> Wizard is already fire-resistant and poison-resistant, so perhaps no
> additional preparations are even needed. Pit traps can be annoying
> however, so I am thinking of polymorphing into a vampire lord (I have
> Polycontrol ring) when it is time to clean the place out. Vampires
> levitate over pits, yet can pick things off the ground. What do you
> think?

Yes, that is a possible approach. But being a Vampire, for example, has
the disadvantage that your first bite-attack on a cockatrice will kill
you instantly.

But once you have an advanced character (and having been in Lucios is
advanced enough) you needn't care too much about pits, trapdoors, and
holes (of course only if you're not going to do the stupid thing of
wielding a cockatrice corpse while walking around).

The worst in your case, the polytraps, might ruin your game; so you
should as soon as possible get MR. In the meantime the ring of poly
control may make such incidents managable. Another bad trap is fire
(you can get that also from magic traps); you should get intrinsic
fire resistance as soon as possible (or by a ring until you have got
the intrisic).

Other traps like water (or fire, once you have the resistance) will
just reduce the effectiveness of your armor or weapons (and destroy
some object types that you best keep in your bag anyway).

A sleeping gas trap might also be annoying, so get the resistance, and
forget this kind of trap.

